# Gear art standard (Idle Party)

Numbers (ink, light, ramps, proportions, gate limits) live only in
`tool/gear_style.py`. This file says what they mean. Do not copy the
numbers into docs or rules.

## One picture

Pixel art on a 128×128 canvas, same origin as the body. One warm ink
contour, never pure black. Light comes from the upper left. Stay on the
material ramp. Detail is a few handmade marks, not a noisy texture.
Silhouettes must still differ at BAG size (26 px) and in the dungeon.

Cloth, leather, mail, and plate stay different surfaces: soft folds,
dark seam rows, a ring checker, hard plate with a highlight and a few
rivets. A hue shift of the same shape is not a new material.

## Model versus copy

A model is one `visualSetId` shape (sword_t0, sword_thunderfury,
helm_ironcrown). Two active models must not share the same icon and the
same paper-doll graphic. A random drop with different stats is not a new
model. Color alone is not a new model. Each model needs its own
silhouette or a handmade hook.

## Icon and doll

The BAG icon is a crop of the same idle overlay the doll paints.
Rarity tint and cloth dye use the same modulate on the icon and the
doll. A class mark shows on the equipped icon when the wearer is known.
BAG with no wearer shows the base model. Boots are the foot band of the
legs overlay, not a second drawing.

## Hard rules

- Owned art under `assets/custom/` only. No foreign dumps.
- One renderer: `paintOwnedHero` and `EquipmentIcon`. No second doll.
- Only `tool/build_owned_gear_layers.py` writes live doll PNGs. New
  scripts write `_src` or `_authored`.
- Face and hair stay on the body. Gear layers do not repaint them.
- No new or removed save fields. Do not rename a `visualSetId`.
- Legacy mappings keep working (old stamps, borrowed weapon stems).
- No `ImageDraw` ellipses or flat placeholders. No hue-only models.
- No upscaled pixel blocks. No hand-edits of `paper_doll_lock.json` or
  `owned_gear_grips.dart`.
- Do not `--relock` over a red facit. Do not lower a gate to go green.
- Do not add entries to `tool/facit_known_debt.json`. Shrink it only
  with `--prune-debt` after a full check.

Workflow: skill `gear-art`.
